From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:57:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 049/162] hjviewer: the iPhone Korean keyboard's own selection
 stays
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A device log of 2026-10-15 (the opt-in keyboard log of patch 0020) shows how
the iOS Korean keyboard edits the hidden field: to compose a syllable and to
delete a jamo it selects the jamo or syllable before the caret and replaces
it, with no composing range. _keepIOSSoftKeyboardCaretAtEnd (patch 0015)
moved the caret to the end as soon as that selection appeared, and broke the
keyboard's edit: 한글입력 typed left ㅎㄴㄱㄹㅇㅂㄹㄱ (the vowels lost), and
every Backspace after the first put the deleted jamo back and deleted it
again, so nothing reached the remote side and the next letter sent the jamo
again.

softKeyboardCaretNeedsMoving keeps a selection that ends at the end and lies
in the typed text; a caret or a selection that ends before the end, or
reaches into the filler (the space-bar trackpad, two keys at once), still
goes back to the end. Tests: the decision on the log's values, and the
select-and-replace steps of composing 한글 and deleting it jamo by jamo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
